<h1>Carmelita Earls</h1>
<p>37th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Filed nominating petitions on Oct. 21, 2026 to challenge Ald. Emma Mitts. No campaign website or platform found.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Retired Chicago Fire Department deputy chief after a 31-year career, a West Side resident for more than 50 years, and a former adjunct professor in the City Colleges system. Elected to the 15th District Police District Council in 2023, which chose her as its chair; listed as a member of the Community Commission for Public Safety and Accountability&#39;s Nominating Committee. Ran for 28th Ward alderman in 2011.</p>
